  "body": "## What happens\n\nAGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" says that a review needs the light lane (`cargo xtask gate light`) on the final head.\n\nThree reviews of P1 PRs in a row do not list that step:\n\n- #3790 review `6033604372` (head `6be6b1265`): no light-lane table. A separate gate run gave it later (6 steps, green).\n- #3802 review (head `c2399c040`): no light-lane table. A separate gate run gave it later (6 steps, green).\n- #3837 review (head `20972341c`): no light-lane table. The PR merged.\n\nEach review lists the pinning tests, the touched binaries and the targeted heavy step. None of them lists the light lane.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe light lane is the only review-time check of the heavy twins. A red twin is a note on the PR, but a missing result is not a pass. A review that omits it hides a red twin.\n\n## Fix\n\nOne of these:\n1. The `PR-reviewer` agent file lists the light lane as a required step with its own line in the report table, and the review comment has a fixed row for it.\n2. The merging session checks for the light-lane row before it flags a PR ready.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe finding comes from the review lane of 2026-11-24. The three PRs above are merged or in review. Their light lanes were green (#3790, #3802) or not run (#3837).\n",
